      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute coronary syndrome after amphetamine use in a young male with myocardial bridging - a case report. A case of a 19-year-old male hospitalised due to acute coronary syndrome following amphetamine use is presented. Coronary angiography revealed the presence of myocardial bridging causing a 90% stenosis of the left anterior descending coronary artery. The patient was treated conservatively and the outcome was uneventful."},
